course: dictionary
lesson: 8098
title: Context clues: remove
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Read the words around an unknown word, because they leave clues. «Wash your hands with soap for about 20 seconds, which removes most germs.» Germs cannot stay on your hands after washing, so remove must mean take away or get rid of.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Washing removes most germs» becomes «Washing takes away most germs», and that still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: Some uses of remove are about safety. «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out; an adult or doctor removes it, because the barb tears skin.» The sentence tells you that removing something can be dangerous, so it is a job for a grown-up.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Remove» is a verb: remove, removes, removed, removing.
fact: «Remove» means to take something away from where it was, to take it off, or to get rid of it.
fact: «Remove your shoes» means take them off, and «remove the label» means take it off.
fact: Only adults should remove splinters, fish hooks or broken glass; if you find some, tell an adult.
exercise: «Zoe removes 4 apples from the basket.» What does removes mean here? | Eats all of them | Counts them twice | *Takes away from the basket | Paints them red
exercise: «Please remove your hat indoors.» What does remove mean? | Buy | Put on | Wash | *Take off
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Charging devices outside the bedroom removes the temptation to play at night» that is a form of remove. | *removes | night | temptation | bedroom
test: Which word means the same as remove in «remove a stain»? | Add | Paint | *Get rid of | Hide
test: Fill the gap: «Yesterday Dad ___ the plates from the table.» | remove | *removed | removes | removing
exam: Fill the gap in «An adult or doctor ___ it, because the barb tears skin.» | *removes | removing | removed | remove
